# Process

How design work gets done on this repo. Written from what actually happened over the design-system
branch, not from an ideal.

---

## The map

```
                    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
                    │  YOU: a defect, a question, or "is this right?" │
                    └───────────────────────┬─────────────────────────┘
                                            ▼
 ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │  1. READ THE SYSTEM FIRST     design.md is normative. Is there already a rule?       │
 │                               Usually there is, buried under another heading.        │
 └───────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                         ▼
 ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │  2. MEASURE, DO NOT ESTIMATE  Open the real page in a real browser. Get numbers.     │
 │                               Measure the PROPERTY, never a proxy for it.            │
 └───────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                         ▼
 ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │  3. AUDIT APP-WIDE            One report is a sample. Find every instance.           │
 │                               "the purchases table" was 15 tables.                   │
 └───────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                         ▼
 ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │  4. PREVIEW                   A mockup in docs/mockups/. Options, each with its      │
 │                               measured cost, a recommendation, and its cons.         │
 └───────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                         ▼
                ╔═══════════════════════╗
                ║  YOU CHOOSE           ║  ◀── the only mandatory stop
                ╚═══════════┬═══════════╝
                            ▼
 ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │  5. BUILD ONCE, CENTRALLY     One controller on the shell beats the same attribute   │
 │                               hand-written into 66 regions.                                 │
 └───────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                         ▼
 ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │  6. VERIFY BY MEASUREMENT     Prove it with the instrument that found the defect.    │
 │        ◀──── disagrees ────   If it disagrees, say so and go back. This happens.     │
 └────────┴──────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                         ▼
 ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │  6a. REVIEW COPY              If it has words: audit, prove the audit ran, then      │
 │                               the judgement half by hand.                            │
 └───────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                         ▼
 ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │  7. SPECS + FULL SUITE        System specs for anything a browser renders.           │
 │                               Then every audit, then the whole suite.                │
 └───────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                         ▼
 ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │  8. DOCUMENT IN THE SAME COMMIT  design.md, changelog, decisions, onboarding,        │
 │                                  domain-model, migration-map, mockup outcome.        │
 └───────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                         ▼
 ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │  9. COMMIT, FILL THE HASH, PUSH  Every checkpoint. The workspace has been reset to   │
 │                                  main underneath the work four times.                │
 └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**In one line:** *read the system → measure → audit everything → preview → you choose → build once →
prove it → document → push.*

---

## How I get pointed at the design system

Nothing here depends on me remembering it. It is written into the repo:

| Where | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `CLAUDE.md` at the repo root | Loaded automatically at the start of every session. Declares **`design.md` is normative — read it before building or changing a screen.** |
| `design.md` | The spec. Every convention, with the measurement that justified it. |
| `app/views/shared/essentials/` and `EssentialsUiHelper` | The components. `CLAUDE.md` says build from these, **not from utility strings**. |
| `docs/migration-map.md` | What is dead. `btn`, `card-body`, `form-group`, `col-md-*`, `fa-*` are defined nowhere and render as nothing. |
| `docs/design-decisions.md` | Why a pattern beat the obvious alternative. Read before re-litigating one. |
| `docs/mockups/` | 24 previews on record, each with the question it answered and what was chosen. |

`CLAUDE.md` also sets the cadence — *work, document, commit, push, at every checkpoint* — and says to
do it **without being asked**. The one thing that still needs asking is a design decision.

---

## The steps

### 1. Read the system first
Grep `design.md` before touching anything. Most defects reported on this branch were **violations of
a rule already written down**, usually filed under a different heading. Two were rules I had broken
myself after writing them.

### 2. Measure, do not estimate
Open the running app and take numbers. Every figure in these documents was measured in the session it
was written.

**The rule that matters most: measure the property, not a proxy for it.** Every serious miss on this
branch was a proxy.

| Proxy that lied | What it missed | The honest instrument |
| --- | --- | --- |
| computed `opacity: 1` | a white fade on a white table — invisible | diff the painted pixels |
| `offsetHeight − clientHeight` | an overlay scrollbar reserves nothing and draws nothing | ask what a person can see |
| axe's declared colours | a gradient painted on top by a pseudo-element | sample the glyph's pixels |
| source text | rendered copy, after `text-transform` | read the DOM as shown |
| a class list | which CSS layer actually wins | computed style |
| `scrollWidth > clientWidth` | page-level overflow | the document's own box |

### 3. Audit app-wide
Never fix only the instance reported. `/purchases` was 15 tables; one inert override was 27 more
views; one tooltip scoped to `.notes` was every clipped cell. The instruments are in `bin/design/`:
`wcag-audit`, `responsive-audit`, `keyboard-audit`, `overlay-audit`, `table-audit`, `page-audit`,
`copy-audit`, `undefined-classes`, `route-sweep`.

### 4. Preview before building a screen
A self-contained HTML mockup in `docs/mockups/`, served by the app. It must carry **the measured
defect**, **two to four real options**, **the cost of each in numbers**, **a recommendation with
reasons**, and **the cons of that recommendation**. Say what you are choosing not to do.

Three traps, each of which has produced a mockup that lied:
- Re-copy `mockup.css` after every Tailwind rebuild — it is a snapshot, not a link.
- A mockup can only use utilities the app already uses. Anything new goes in its own `<style>` block.
- The app's own stylesheet still applies. Switch off any rule you are proposing to replace.

### 5. Build once, centrally
Prefer one Stimulus controller on the shell to the same attribute hand-written into 66
regions across 62 views. It survives Turbo, it
cannot drift, and there is one place to fix.

### 6. Verify by measurement
Re-run the instrument that found the defect. **When it disagrees with me, it wins.** Several claims
were corrected mid-flight this way, including two of my own contrast figures and three audits that
were checking the wrong thing.

Watch for the three quiet failures: a **rule that does not apply** because a utility beat it, a
**spec that passes for the wrong reason**, and a **mockup that lies**.

### 6a. Review copy, if the change has words in it
Copy is reviewed like code and in a fixed order — see **Reviewing copy** in `design.md`. The short
version: run `copy-audit.rb`, then **plant a violation to prove it read your files**, then do the
judgement half by hand (a subtitle that defines its title, a button whose verb is not what happens,
a claim that is not true of the code). Verify claims by opening the view, not by grepping — an empty
grep and a missing feature look identical. And check the **partner portal separately**: it is a
second product with a second audience, and sweeping the bank side feels like finishing.

### 7. Specs and the full suite
System specs for anything a browser renders — request specs do not run JavaScript, and three classes
of defect on this branch were invisible to everything but the browser suite. Then, every time:

```
bundle exec rubocop && bundle exec erb_lint --lint-all
ruby bin/design/page-audit.rb && python3 bin/design/undefined-classes.py
pw bin/design/wcag-audit.js         # axe, 156 pages
pw bin/design/responsive-audit.js   # 1,573 page/width combinations
pw bin/design/keyboard-audit.js
pw bin/design/overlay-audit.js
pw bin/design/table-audit.js
bundle exec rspec                   # the whole suite, about 9 minutes
```

### 8. Document in the same commit
Not afterwards. A stale document is worse than none, because the next person trusts it.

| Document | When |
| --- | --- |
| `design.md` | A component, token, layout or convention changed. |
| `docs/changelog.md` | **Always.** One row: the commit, and what changed, in a sentence that still means something in a year. |
| `docs/design-decisions.md` | A judgement call worth explaining, with the alternatives rejected. |
| `docs/domain-model.md` | A model, association, enum or role changed. Verify with `rails runner`. |
| `docs/migration-map.md` | Something migrated, retired, or found as a leftover. |
| `docs/onboarding.md` | Setup, testing conventions, **or anything a user sees**. Its user half goes stale quietly. |
| `docs/architecture/decisions/` | A structural decision. Add or supersede; never rewrite what a past one said. |
| `docs/mockups/README.md` | The outcome of the preview: what was chosen, and what building it found. |

### 9. Commit, fill the hash, push
The changelog row needs the hash of its own commit, so: commit → read the hash → write it in →
commit that → push. **Push at every checkpoint.** This workspace has been reset to `main` underneath
the work four times; nothing was lost only because everything was already pushed.

---

## What the process is for

Three things it produces that ad-hoc work does not:

1. **A defect is fixed everywhere it exists**, because step 3 is not optional.
2. **The reasoning outlives the reasoner.** The number that justified a rule sits next to the rule, so
   the next person can tell whether it still holds.
3. **Claims are falsifiable.** Everything asserted was measured, and when it turned out to be wrong it
   was corrected in the open.

The failure mode it exists to prevent: **a check that reads a proxy reports what the proxy says.**
Every browser audit here has, at least once, reported clean while the defect you reported was
live: axe across 156 pages while the pinned column sat at 3.19:1, the keyboard and responsive
audits while a scrollbar drew nothing at all, and responsive again while all fifteen tables showed
a fifth of themselves at 320px.
